@startuml UC-003-analysis-sequence
!include ../../../diagrams/style.iuml
title UC-003 Execute target model: analysis sequence diagram

actor Developer
boundary "Progress Listener" as PLis
control "Execute Target" as Exec
entity "Benchmark" as B
entity "Target Result" as TR
boundary "Target Model Interface" as TMI
actor "Target model" as TM

note over Exec
  Triggered inside a run (UC-006), with a loaded
  benchmark (UC-002) and a target connection (UC-001).
end note

[-> Exec : execute(benchmark, target)
Exec -> B : get test cases, in order
B --> Exec : test cases
loop for each test case, in benchmark order
  alt the run has not been stopped
    Exec -> TMI : send(question), once
    TMI -> TM : question
    alt main success scenario: the target replies (3a: also a refusal or a cut-off answer)
      TM --> TMI : model response
      TMI --> Exec : model response
      Exec -> TR : create(test case, model response)
    else 2a: a connector error (unavailable, rate limit, ...)
      TM --> TMI : error
      TMI --> Exec : connector error
      Exec -> TR : create(test case, connector error)
      Exec -> Exec : carry on with the next case
    else 2b: an auth or quota error
      TM --> TMI : error
      TMI --> Exec : connector error
      Exec -> TR : create(test case, connector error)
      Exec -> Exec : stop the run (set the stop reason)
    else 2c: anything else fails (a bug in the target code)
      TMI --> Exec : unexpected failure
      [<-- Exec : the bug escapes unchanged;\nno results are returned
    end
  else the run was stopped by an earlier case
    Exec -> TR : create(test case, error "not sent: run\nstopped after ... on case ...")
  end
  Exec -> PLis : case executed(target result)
  PLis -> Developer : progress
end
[<-- Exec : target results, one per case,\nin benchmark order (judged in UC-004)

note right of TR
  Exactly one of model response and connector
  error is present. A refusal or cut-off answer
  is still a model response (3a).
end note
@enduml
